# Apple HIG & Glassmorphism UI Rules

## Theme palette
- Support dark and light themes, plus following the Windows system theme.
- Dark surfaces: `#000000`, `#1C1C1E`, `#2C2C2E`; light surfaces: `#F2F2F7`, `#FFFFFF`, `#E5E5EA`.
- Accent color: `#007AFF`.
- Prefer translucent surfaces, restrained blur, soft shadows, and rounded corners where they improve hierarchy and readability.

## Typography and contrast
- Use standard UI fonts, a clear type hierarchy, and high contrast against every background.
- Dropdowns, context menus, menus, and popups must set their background and foreground explicitly for the active theme: dark surfaces with white text in dark mode, white surfaces with black text in light mode.
- Hover and selection states use a blue accent with readable foreground text. Disabled items remain legible in light gray or an equivalent high-contrast theme color.
- Never use white-on-white, black-on-black, or gray-on-gray text.

## Layout
- Use responsive Grid rows and columns, with sufficient margins and padding to prevent clipped text, overlap, or truncated labels.
- Keep badges wide enough for localized text and preserve readable spacing when values change language or length.

## Efficient changes
- Make focused patch-style edits; do not rewrite unchanged files.
- Keep user-facing replies concise and include relevant verification results.
